    "created_at": "2019-03-26T08:06:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-03-26T08:06:22Z",
    "body": "The nested `<p>` tags is in the expected features since XML5 wouldn’t have the HTML `<p>` tag auto‑close behavuour, since the XML parser is unaffected by the namespace, so it stands to reason that you could nest `<p>` tags.\r\n```xml\r\n<div>\r\n  <p>\r\n  <p>\r\n  <p>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\nWould result in:\r\n```xml\r\n<div>\r\n └ <p>\r\n    └ <p>\r\n       └ <p>\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
